[{"id":2772639919,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6lQyCv","state":"APPROVED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?u=af70f5d107e9c1447f296643d5a566dab53d25e8&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","login":"AThousandShips","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips"},"body":"Difficult to test in depth but the code makes sense and covers all the cases here","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105453#pullrequestreview-2772639919","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105453","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2025-04-16T13:58:04Z"},{"id":2772802078,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6lRZoe","state":"APPROVED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11797174?u=a254c0fcd6cf4668367407a460e175559e12dc6f&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/RandomShaper","id":11797174,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzk3MTc0","login":"RandomShaper","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper"},"body":"Looks good.\r\n\r\nIf anything, I'd suggest making the determination of the class being thread-safe for signals or not static at compile time.\r\n\r\nSomething like this (`GDCLASS` would still need to be usable with two arguments, but you get the idea):\r\n```C++\r\n#define THREAD_SAFE_SIGNALS_FUNC_false \\\r\n    struct _ObjectSignalLock { \\\r\n        _ObjectSignalLock(void *) {} \\\r\n    };\r\n\r\n#define THREAD_SAFE_SIGNALS_FUNC_true \\\r\n    Mutex signal_mutex; \\\r\n    \\\r\n    struct _ObjectSignalLock { \\\r\n\tMutexLock lock; \\\r\n\t_ObjectSignalLock(const Object *const p_obj) : lock(p_obj.signal_mutex) {} \\\r\n};\r\n\r\n#define GDCLASS(m_class, m_inherits, m_thread_safe_signals) \\\r\n    /* [...] */ \\\r\n    THREAD_SAFE_SIGNALS_FUNC_##m_thread_safe_signals \\\r\n    /* [...] */\r\n```\r\n\r\nThat way, we'd remove the allocation and the subsequent indirection for the mutex, as well as runtime branching. `OBJ_SIGNAL_LOCK` would just be either a direct lock or no-op for non-signal-thread-safe classes.\r\n\r\nIn any case, I'm considering this an optimization that can be tackled later or by someone else.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105453#pullrequestreview-2772802078","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105453","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2025-04-16T14:42:04Z"},{"id":2772814687,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6lRctf","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11797174?u=a254c0fcd6cf4668367407a460e175559e12dc6f&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/RandomShaper","id":11797174,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzk3MTc0","login":"RandomShaper","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper"},"body":"I forgot to add that these should be under the lock as well:\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105453/files#diff-7b1b6d9ebe2a4eabbafa4ee69f0aad4bf988539e4fe84c0f5f3bcfec78d9a8d2R2263-R2290","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105453#pullrequestreview-2772814687","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105453","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2025-04-16T14:45:01Z"},{"id":2773475770,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6lT-G6","state":"APPROVED","co